This PR is mostly about adding support for the Inspector v1 `additionalNodes` option as well as handling properties for objects with `inspectableCustomProperties`.

1. `additionalNodes` - this just adds a Scene Explorer extension (service definition) to add the static set of nodes specified by this option.
2. `inspectableCustomProperties` - this always needs to be present, even if we are not invoking Inspector v2 through the new APIs. Otherwise, objects that have this property will not show up in Inspector v2, which we don't want. Because of this, I moved ./backCompat.tsx to ./legacy/inspector.tsx (contains the legacy `Inspector` static class), moved ./debugLayer.ts to ./legacy/debugLayer.ts, and added `inspectableCustomPropertiesService.ts` to the legacy folder as well. This way, all "legacy" support is organized in the legacy folder. inspectableCustomPropertiesService.ts exports a service definition that is always included in Inspector v2 though.

Here is an example that combines both `additionalNodes` and custom inspectable objects:
```ts
Inspector.Show(scene, {
    additionalNodes: [
        {
            name: "test",
            getContent: () => [
                {
                    name: "item",
                    getClassName: () => "item class name",
                    _checkboxProp1: true,
                    get checkboxProp1() {
                        return (this as any)._checkboxProp1;
                    },
                    set checkboxProp1(value: boolean) {
                        console.log("set checkboxProp1:", value);
                        (this as any)._checkboxProp1 = value;
                    },
                    sliderProp1: 42,
                    vector3Prop1: new Vector3(1, 2, 3),
