6.29.2.description:
- Unify dot and normalize APIs for Vector2, Vector3, Vector4, Vector2, Quaternion
- Add the BetweenTwoVectors method to Unger


The benefit of the unified API is that you can make indiscriminate calls to the union types of Vector2, Vector3, Vector4, Vector2, Quaternion, as follows:
```ts
public static BetweenTwoVectors<Vec extends Vector2 | Vector3 | Vector4>(a: DeepImmutable<Vec>, b: DeepImmutable<Vec>): Angle {
        const na = a.normalizeToNew() as Vec;
        const nb = b.normalizeToNew() as Vec;
        let cosv = na.dot(nb as any);
        cosv = Scalar.Clamp(cosv, -1, 1);
        const theta = Math.acos(cosv);
        return new Angle(theta);
}
```

